\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Leaving the interval is punished with a very low tanh function.
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A conceivable solution would be to use a constantly increasing weighting
 function, such as tanh or log, as a distance to the edge area, to greatly
 reduce the influence of the values.
 However, it must be meticulously observed that the distance function is
 misused by a too large second factor, which would lead to a complete misinterpr
etation of candidates.
 If the proportion of candidates who could overcome this artificially generated
 second factor is not large enough, the genetic selection process is obsolete.
 The proportion of this punishment to the final value becomes an error factor
 within the regression, which is already a surrogate model.
\end_layout

